  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 14,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.736,
            0.047,
            0.847,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Number Play"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.085,
            0.791,
            0.187
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 1,
              "bbox": [
                0.207,
                0.085,
                0.791,
                0.187
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_14_table_1.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>n = 5</td><td>1 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 11 + 1 + 1 + 21 + 1 + 2 + 11 + 2 + 1 + 11 + 2 + 2</td><td>2 + 1 + 1 + 12 + 1 + 22 + 2 + 1</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.197,
            0.593,
            0.216
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, there are 8 rhythms having 5 beats!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.216,
            0.849,
            0.345
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The reason this method works is that every 5-beat rhythm must begin with either a "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "^ { \\circ } 1 + ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " or a "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "^ { \\circ } 2 + ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . If it begins with a "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "^ { \\circ } 1 + ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , then the remaining numbers must give a 4-beat rhythm, and we can write all those down. If it begins with a "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 + ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , then the remaining number must give a 3-beat rhythm, and we can write all those down. Therefore, the number of 5-beat rhythms is the number of 4-beat rhythms, plus the number of 3-beat rhythms."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.345,
            0.848,
            0.402
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How many 6-beat rhythms are there? By the same reasoning, it will be the number of 5-beat rhythms plus the number of 4-beat rhythms, i.e., "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "8+5=13"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Thus, there are 13 rhythms having 6 beats."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.409,
            0.847,
            0.451
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Use the systematic method to write down all 6-beat rhythms, i.e., write 6 as the sum of 1’s and 2’s in all possible ways. Did you get 13 ways?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.458,
            0.849,
            0.608
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This beautiful method for counting all the rhythms of short syllables and long syllables having any given number of beats was first given by the great Prakrit scholar "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Virahāṅka",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " around the year 700 CE. He gave his method in the form of a Prakrit poem! For this reason, the sequence 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, 21, 34, . . . is known as the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Virahāṅka sequence",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", and the numbers in the sequence are known as the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Virahāṅka numbers",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Virahāṅka",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " was the first known person in history to explicitly consider these important numbers and write down the rule for their formation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.607,
            0.848,
            0.699
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Other scholars in India also considered these numbers in the same poetic context. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Virahāṅka",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " was inspired by earlier work of the legendary Sanskrit scholar Piṅgala, who lived around 300 BCE. After "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Virahāṅka",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", these numbers were also written about by Gopala (c. 1135 CE) and then by Hemachandra (c. 1150 CE)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.699,
            0.849,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the West, these numbers have been known as the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fibonacci numbers",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", after the Italian mathematician who wrote about them in the year 1202 CE — about 500 years after "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Virahāṅka",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". As we can see, Fibonacci was not first, nor the second, not even the third person to write about these numbers! Sometimes the term “"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Virahāṅka",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "–Fibonacci numbers” is used so that everyone understands what is being referred to."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.827,
            0.847,
            0.883
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, how many rhythms of short and long syllables are there having 8 beats? We simply take the 8th element of the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Virahāṅka",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " sequence: 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, 21, 34 , 55, ..."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.883,
            0.602,
            0.903
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, there are 34 rhythms having 8 beats."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.808,
            0.938,
            0.844,
            0.955
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "141"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
